<!--
  ============================================================================
  Warcasket_BuildPathCut.xml                 Jawa_Armoury · authored 2026-08-12
  ============================================================================

  THE DECISION THIS IMPLEMENTS
  ============================
  faction_roster_v2.md §12, open question 1, DECIDED 2026-08-11 by the owner:

      "a Jawa could only wear a scavenged suit, and even then that's a
       hilarious image and too cool to say no to."

  YES to wearing a warcasket, but only a SALVAGED shell. Never a built one.
  Building one from raw material is out-of-order power (Axis 18); cutting one
  off a corpse is the Jawa economy working as intended.

  ⚠️ READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE JOB IS DONE
  ============================================
  THIS FILE ONLY CLOSES BUILDING. IT DOES NOT OPEN SALVAGE. Those are two
  separate jobs and only the first one is cheap.

  Per §12 Q1, a dead warcasket is unrecoverable by FOUR independent mechanisms:
  destroyOnDrop on VFEP_WarcasketPartBase; VFEPirates.GenSpawn_Spawn_Patch
  returning false for any WarcasketDef on the root GenSpawn.Spawn overload;
  ThingDef::PlayerAcquirable false with no <thingCategories>, so no stockpile or
  bill filter can see them; and DropAll skipping IsLocked apparel, which
  warcaskets always are. Butchering a casketed corpse yields ChunkSlagSteel.

  So as of today there is NO salvaged path to preserve. Deploying this file
  alone leaves the player with no warcasket access whatsoever. That is a
  defensible interim state — it is strictly closer to the owner's decision than
  the status quo, which allows free manufacture — but it must be a CONSCIOUS
  choice, not a surprise. The salvaged shell has to be built (the fusion bench,
  §12 item 2, feasible only as a custom Building_Enterable in C#).

  WHERE THE CHOKE POINT ACTUALLY IS  [audited 2026-08-12, from the files]
  ======================================================================
  Read from the installed mods, not assumed:

    * VFEP_WarcasketFoundry is the ONLY warcasket production building in the
      load set. Buildings_Production.xml declares exactly one non-abstract
      ThingDef under VFEP_FoundryBase, at designationCategory Production,
      researchPrerequisites VFEP_Warcaskets.

    * Every warcasket piece — INCLUDING the helmet — is a
      VFEPirates.WarcasketDef, not a ThingDef. They carry <costList> and
      <researchPrerequisites>, which the foundry UI consumes. NONE of them has
      a <recipeMaker>, so there is no bench route and no bill to remove.
      (The two <recipeMaker> blocks in VFEP's Apparel_Various.xml belong to the
      privateer armour and the rumsuit, which are unrelated.)

    * WarCasket Expanded (Aoba.WarCasket, 2733135485) ships ONE def file,
      1.6/Defs/Apparel_Various.xml, containing only VFEPirates.WarcasketDef
      entries. Zero ResearchProjectDefs, zero buildings. It rides on VFEP's
      foundry and VFEP's research.

    * Farhan's Warcasket Tweaks (3533261706) and VFE Pirates – Hardworking
      Warcaskets (dmp.vfepirates.warcasketwork, 3535194807) are patch-only.
      The latter ships exactly ApparelPatches.xml and TraitPatches.xml.

  Therefore removing the foundry from the build menu closes the player build
  path across ALL FOUR mods. There is no second route to plug.

  TWO MORE MODS REFERENCE VFEP_Warcaskets. A whole-workshop sweep (2026-08-12)
  found exactly five folders mentioning it. Neither extra one changes the above,
  but both are recorded so the sweep does not have to be repeated:

    * Oracle's Miscellania (oracle.miscellania, 3279582979) — NOT ACTIVE in the
      568 list. Its 1.6/Mods/VFE.Pirates/ conditional folder adds three more
      VFEPirates.WarcasketDef pieces (VFEP_Warcasket_EarthEmpire and friends).
      No building, no recipe. If it is ever activated, this cut still covers it,
      because it too can only be produced at the foundry.

    * Nice Research Tab (Andromeda.NiceResearchTab, 3773496046) — ACTIVE at 450.
      A research-tab LAYOUT mod; it names VFEP_Warcaskets in a FineTune def to
      position the node. It grants nothing and adds no route. It loads at 450
      and we patch at 563, so our relabelled node is what it lays out. If the
      node ever renders with the ORIGINAL label, NRT is caching def text at a
      point we do not win — check there before suspecting op 2 failed.

  NPC JUNKERS ARE UNTOUCHED, WHICH IS THE ENTIRE POINT. They get their caskets
  from PawnKinds_Junkers.xml, and pawnkind generation never consults research or
  designationCategory. The Junkers keep walking around in the armour the player
  cannot make — which is exactly the tension the faction was designed for.

  WHY designationCategory AND NOT DELETING THE RESEARCH NODE
  ==========================================================
  §12 says "cutting that one node closes the entire player build path", and it
  is right about the topology. But REMOVING a ResearchProjectDef is the wrong
  tool: VFEP_AdvancedWarcaskets lists it in <prerequisites>, and 45 defs across
  VFEP and Expanded list it in <researchPrerequisites>. Deleting it converts a
  clean cut into a wall of "Could not resolve cross-reference" — the def-loader
  error, i.e. a live mod-set problem, not a save problem.

  Clearing <designationCategory> is the technique already PROVEN in this stack:
  it is how the droid factory was removed from the build menu, confirmed working
  in play 2026-08-11. It breaks no references, it is one operation, and it is
  reversible by deleting this file.

  Op 2 exists so the cut is not a TRAP. With the foundry unbuildable, finishing
  VFEP_Warcaskets grants literally nothing — the node gates the foundry plus
  three apparel groups, and those groups can only be produced at the foundry. A
  player would spend 3000 research points on an empty box. Verified safe to
  rewrite: VFEP ships a Languages/English folder with NO DefInjected directory,
  so nothing re-overrides our label or description after patching.

  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  =====================
  Positions read from runtime/backups/ModsConfig.full-568.2026-08-11.xml:

      470  oskarpotocki.vfe.pirates           <- defines both targets
      485  farhanfair.warcaskettweakspatch
      501  dmp.vfepirates.warcasketwork
      502  aoba.warcasket
      563  mandrake.rsw.armoury              <- us, after all four ✅

  Wrapped in PatchOperationFindMod so the whole file is a silent no-op if VFE
  Pirates is ever removed. Each op is additionally PatchOperationConditional on
  the exact node, so a VFEP update that restructures either def makes this fall
  silent rather than fail.

  ⚠️ Both guards return TRUE when they match nothing (see traps.md,
  "PatchOperationFindMod(X) failed"). A clean log is therefore NOT evidence this
  worked. Only the build menu is.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Architect > Production: NO "warcasket foundry". That is the whole test.
    * Research tab: the "warcaskets (salvaged shells only)" node is present,
      researchable, and its description says plainly that it grants no foundry.
    * Dev-spawn a VFEP_Footsoldier: still fully casketed. If the Junkers lost
      their armour, this file hit pawnkind generation and must be reverted.
    * grep Player.log for "Could not resolve cross-reference" — baseline 28.
      A jump means the research node was reached after all.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- 1. THE CUT. Remove the only warcasket production building from the
                architect menu. Everything else in this file is signposting. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketFoundry"]/designationCategory</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEP_WarcasketFoundry"]/designationCategory</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- 2. Do not leave a 3000-point research node that grants nothing.
                Label and description only; the node itself stays, because 45
                defs and one downstream project reference it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="VFEP_Warcaskets"]/label</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="VFEP_Warcaskets"]/label</xpath>
            <value>
              <label>warcaskets (salvaged shells only)</label>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="VFEP_Warcaskets"]/description</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="VFEP_Warcaskets"]/description</xpath>
            <value>
              <description>Understand how a warcasket is welded shut around a living pilot.\n\nThis knowledge does NOT let the clan build one. Warcasket foundries are Junker work, and their machining tolerances are far beyond anything a scavenger crew can fabricate from scrap. No foundry can be constructed.\n\nWhat it buys is the ability to recognise, strip and eventually re-seat a shell cut off a dead Junker. A Jawa in a dead man's armour is the only warcasket this clan will ever field.</description>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
